{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Of the fruit of the ground.</b> He should have brought first-fruits from the fruit of the tree, of the seven species; but Scripture tells of his baseness and his miserliness, for he was a man of evil eye. This is why it does not say 'of the first of the fruit of the ground' but rather 'of the fruit of the ground' — that is, from the least of all; and it was flax seed, as the Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted. And the verses indicate as much, for therefore it is brief regarding his meal-offering, which was not accepted, and lengthy regarding the meal-offering of Abel, which was accepted; and this is what it says: 'of the firstborn of his flock and of their fat' — for Abel brought first-fruits of a thing fit for an offering, while Cain brought fruits that are not fit for an offering, and not the first fruits but the least of the fruits. Thus they interpreted in the Midrash: like a servant who eats the first-fruits and sends the gleanings to the king — that is, the last ones. The Jerusalem Targum: ובקטן כלה סייף." "<b>A meal-offering to HaShem.</b> This meal-offering was on day fifty of the creation of the world, both according to the words of Rabbi Eliezer and according to the words of Rabbi Yehoshua. And thus the Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted in Bereshit Rabbah: 'of the fruit of the ground — a meal-offering.' Rabbi Eliezer and Rabbi Yehoshua: Rabbi Eliezer says, 'In Tishrei the world was created'; Rabbi Yehoshua says, 'In Nisan the world was created.' And it says there: all agree, whether according to this one or according to that one, Abel did not endure in the world except fifty days." "<b>And from the fact</b> that these two Sages were precise about fifty days, there emerges for us a reason why we were commanded in the Torah to bring a meal-offering on the day of Assembly (Atzeret) corresponding to Cain and Abel, who brought a meal-offering on day fifty; for through that meal-offering the truth of prophecy will be verified, and that is what is written: 'And HaShem said to Cain.' And the providence will be verified, also the punishment and the reward — all is included there." "<b>And you should</b> reflect from here upon the wonders of the Almighty, how He is precise in exacting punishment and reward, for He shows favor to no man such that He would not punish him, and He does not withhold the reward of any such that He would not requite him. For behold Abel, who was killed on day fifty, received his reward, and Moses was elevated to receive the Torah on day fifty. And Cain, who killed on day fifty, was cursed on that very day; and his strength, which is the evil inclination, is destined to be punished and annulled from the world on day fifty of the Holy One, blessed be He, of whom it is written (Psalms 90:4): ״כי אלף שנים בעיניך כיו אתמול״ and so forth. And all is measure for measure from Him, blessed be His name, in whose hand is the soul of all that lives, and who punishes them and requites them according to His will, and all is justice, for His are the balance and scales of justice. And from this the Torah forbade leaven in the meal-offering, for it alludes to the evil inclination, and Scripture says in all cases: ״לא תאפה חמץ״; but on day fifty He explicitly commanded (Leviticus 23:17): ״חמץ תאפינה״. Because day fifty of Assembly (Atzeret) corresponds to the great Jubilee of the world, when the evil inclination will be uprooted and its memory obliterated. And understand this."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :register {:flags {3 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {3 "Printed source cites (ויקרא טו) for the verse חמץ תאפינה; the correct citation for Leviticus 23:17 has been normalized. The citation (תהילים צ׳:ד׳) is Psalms 90:4."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:13.567053553Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}